    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6656" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cappăris</span></b> , is,
		f. (acc. -im, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1,
			1, 90</span></i>; Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 79</span></i>
		P.; acc. -in, <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
		9</span></i>), and (rare) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cappă-ri</span></b> , indecl.
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάππαρις</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάππαρι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the caper-bush</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 11,
				3, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 3,
				54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 23, 44, § 127</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Oct. 11, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capparis cortex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 17, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The fruit of the caper-bush</i>, <i>the caper</i>, Plaut. l. l.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capparin et cepas voras, Mart. l. l.: urinam
					movet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					2, 31</span></i>
			.</div>
